{
  "_comment": "The Wayfinder's keywords (game/keywords.py; design: claude/design-brisering-keywords.md). A trip is three words, one per slot, like .hack's Chaos Gates (user, 2026-11-19): danger, then land, then feature. The same three words always lead to the same place (layout fixed by the words); what's in it is rolled each trip. EVERY WORD HERE IS A PLACEHOLDER until the user writes the real vocabulary. GRAMMAR (user, 2026-11-19): danger and land words are each an adjective or a verb (pos: adjective or verb; verbs are written as -ing words, like Dancing); a place can't have a verb for both its danger and its land word (both adjectives is fine); feature words are nouns (pos: noun; a noun phrase is fine, like Victory Lap). Valid: [Hungry][Tangled][Victory Lap], [Dancing][Green][Ropeway]. Invalid: [Singing][Listing][Ideas]. Ids are lowercase; 'word' is how it's shown, in brackets. danger words: danger 1-5 (creature tiers, how rare the find is) and depth (number of areas, 1-5). land words: style (caves, ruins, forest, mountains, plains), light (sky: under the open sky, lit when its half of the Overland faces the star, so it follows the Duel; or dark: sheltered, always dark, torchlight only; v0.93.0, was day or torch), area_size [width, height]. feature words (every key optional): light (lit or dark: fixes the light whatever the land and the Duel, the miasma's doing), creatures (a multiplier on how many), favour (a creature id that turns up far more often, wherever it lives, if the danger allows its tier), rarity_up (the find is rolled as if the danger were this much higher), writings (a multiplier on the chance of a writing in each area). start: the words known at a new game. rank_words: words the Guild teaches a Hunter who rises to that rank (index into data/ranks.json). v0.67.0 (user, Chapter 1): Murmuring (danger 3), Specter's (caves, dark), Broken Promise (creatures halved, sight: light reaches 20% less far). Taught only by the chapter. v0.70.0 (user's additions; effects the user didn't give are the assistant's): any word may carry effects now, combined across the three words: creatures (multiplied), favour, rarity_up, rarity_chance (chance the prize is one rarity higher), writings, sight, items [[item id, least, most], ...] (extra finds in each area), time (turns per step: 2 = half speed), alert (creatures awake and always noticing you), only (the only creature, any tier, anywhere). A land word can give styles {style: weight} instead of style: each area rolls its terrain, fixed by the words. Styles: caves, ruins, forest, mountains, plains, grassland, marsh.",
